KG42.register("clusters-3cd4f200b0b96922ea8832f6",{"id":"46-commercial_building_transactive_control::v142-d-K004","paper":"46-commercial_building_transactive_control","label":"Implementation from the central air-conditioning clearing price to the setpoint and chilled-air volume","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K004","label":"Implementation from the central air-conditioning clearing price to the setpoint and chilled-air volume","market_meaning":"The air-market clearing price is mapped to form the cooling setpoint, and the local temperature-control loop then adjusts the chilled-air supply to implement the clearing quantity for each zone and the market; baseline fallback and insufficient-flexibility handling retain their respective reported conditions.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["pricing","coordination","activation"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"The scope is limited to the coordination and implementation of central air-conditioning clearing results. The preference, privacy, and configuration clauses of R002 are still retained, but different price roles and exceptional situations cannot be regarded as already unified; the overlapping representation of timing configuration is separately shared by reference through K008.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Price conversion and local-loop execution jointly connect market results and physical supply, with clear responsible activities and target results; price calculation serves only as an interface, and no scientific dependency edge is added based on narrative order.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Primary responsibility for the coordination from clearing price to setpoint, preference setting, and fallback behavior under each reported condition."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Primary responsibility for the procedural execution in which the local temperature-control loop implements the updated setpoint as chilled-air supply."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"References the source of the clearing price and the corresponding reported branch, without separately owning the price-return rule."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E025","v141-b-g01-e09"],"rationale":"Only within the air-market scope, map the clearing price output to the price input of Step 3; electricity, water, and air prices are not treated as equivalent to one another."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::x::x_T_set"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09"],"rationale":"The same Step 3 explicitly states that after the setpoint is updated, the local temperature-control loop adjusts the chilled-air supply to achieve the clearing quantity; this connection retains only its original procedural meaning."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"evidence_ids":["ev-v141-b-g03-013"],"rationale":"The two Rule-Chains respectively retain the clearing-price result and the baseline-equivalent setpoint result of the same reported worked example, forming complementary descriptions of that case and not extending to a general clearing theorem."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g04-E01","v141-b-g04-E02","v141-b-g04-E03"],"rationale":"The load-following insufficient-flexibility case explicitly links the minimum clearing price with the minimum cooling setpoint, and the two Rule-Chains cover the price handling and its setpoint consequence; this is not generalized to all no-intersection situations."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R002::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E025","v141-b-g01-e09"],"rationale":"Both places reference the same price functional node; the representative selection does not resolve the quantity identity of commodity prices or historical average prices."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R003::V::clearing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::V::clearing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E025","v141-b-g01-e09"],"rationale":"Both reference the existing clearing function, involving price return and result execution respectively; price output and clearing quantity are not merged on this basis."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G01","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The relationship between the electricity-price input in Eq. (1) and the chilled-air clearing price in Step 3 is not clear; the historical average electricity price and the same-symbol clearing price in the reported worked example also lack independent identity closure.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::theta_lambda_t","v141-c-R002::theta::theta_lambda_hat_mean","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C008","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e13","ev-v141-b-g03-013"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g02-P01"],"required_work":"Verify commodity price transfer and symbol scope, and separately clarify the mapped input, the historical statistic, and the case clearing output; the mapping proposal remains pending review, and no new price equation is added."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G02","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The no-intersection fallback to baseline, the baseline equivalence in the reported case, and the minimum setpoint under insufficient flexibility belong to different conditions; neither the priority when these conditions overlap nor the definition of the minimum value is given.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C007","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E037","ev-v141-b-g03-013","v141-b-g04-E01","v141-b-g04-E02"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Clarify the service, trigger conditions, coverage order, and source-supported price and setpoint bounds of each branch; do not combine different cases into a unified fallback."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G03","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R003 does not freeze the per-zone clearing quantity, the market total, or the local-loop dynamics and error relationships; the procedural implementation description cannot prove exact equality at any time or a tracking guarantee.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::E::v141-c-R003-E001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If quantitative closed-loop rules are needed, supplement upstream the clearing quantity, execution quantity, and loop relationships supported by the source; currently only the qualitative execution obligation is retained."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G04","category":"unverified_source","description":"The evidence for setpoint conversion, case branches, and execution relationships remains unverified, and independent transcription or scientific verification has not yet been performed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g02-E037","ev-v141-b-g03-013","v141-b-g04-E02"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequently verify Step 3, Eq. (1), and the corresponding case paragraphs, and separately check the general mechanism and the case conclusions."}]},"rule_refs":["46-commercial_building_transactive_control::v141-c-R002","46-commercial_building_transactive_control::v141-c-R003","46-commercial_building_transactive_control::v141-c-R004"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-2922a59013d1b13e","COMP-af3f5366a613b34d","COMP-c08cf41f234ed625","COMP-f25a5df437fc6d4f"]});
